\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Thirteen: Nature, the Enjoyer and Consciousness\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/\",\"bb\":3207,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/5/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 5\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/8-12/\",\"title\":\"TEXTS 8-12\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":3640,\"bb\":568354,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"महाभूतान्यहङ्कारो बुद्धिरव्यक्तमेव च ।
इन्द्रियाणि दशैकं च पञ्च चेन्द्रियगोचरा: ॥ ६ ॥
इच्छा द्वेष: सुखं दु:खं सङ्घातश्चेतना धृति: ।
एतत्क्षेत्रं समासेन सविकारमुदाहृतम् ॥ ७ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3641,\"bb\":3208,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3208/\",\"body_value\":\"mahā-bhūtāny ahaṅkāro
buddhir avyaktam eva ca
indriyāṇi daśaikaṁ ca
pañca cendriya-gocarāḥ\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3642,\"bb\":3209,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3209/\",\"body_value\":\"icchā dveṣaḥ sukhaṁ duḥkhaṁ
saṅghātaś cetanā dhṛtiḥ
etat kṣetraṁ samāsena
sa-vikāram udāhṛtam\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3643,\"bb\":3210,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3210/\",\"shadow_value\":\"mahā-bhūtāni – the great elements; ahaṅkāraḥ – false ego; buddhiḥ – intelligence; avyaktam – the unmanifested; eva – certainly; ca – also; indriyāṇi – the senses; daśa-ekam – eleven; ca – also; pañca – five; ca – also; indriya-go-carāḥ – the objects of the senses; icchā – desire; dveṣaḥ – hatred; sukham – happiness; duḥkham – distress; saṅghātaḥ – the aggregate; cetanā – living symptoms; dhṛtiḥ – conviction; etat – all this; kṣetram – the field of activities; samāsena – in summary; sa-vikāram – with interactions; udāhṛtam – exemplified.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"mahā-bhūtāni\",\"translation\":\"the great elements\"},{\"word\":\"ahaṅkāraḥ\",\"translation\":\"false ego\"},{\"word\":\"buddhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"intelligence\"},{\"word\":\"avyaktam\",\"translation\":\"the unmanifested\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"indriyāṇi\",\"translation\":\"the senses\"},{\"word\":\"daśa-ekam\",\"translation\":\"eleven\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"pañca\",\"translation\":\"five\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"indriya-go-carāḥ\",\"translation\":\"the objects of the senses\"},{\"word\":\"icchā\",\"translation\":\"desire\"},{\"word\":\"dveṣaḥ\",\"translation\":\"hatred\"},{\"word\":\"sukham\",\"translation\":\"happiness\"},{\"word\":\"duḥkham\",\"translation\":\"distress\"},{\"word\":\"saṅghātaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the aggregate\"},{\"word\":\"cetanā\",\"translation\":\"living symptoms\"},{\"word\":\"dhṛtiḥ\",\"translation\":\"conviction\"},{\"word\":\"etat\",\"translation\":\"all this\"},{\"word\":\"kṣetram\",\"translation\":\"the field of activities\"},{\"word\":\"samāsena\",\"translation\":\"in summary\"},{\"word\":\"sa-vikāram\",\"translation\":\"with interactions\"},{\"word\":\"udāhṛtam\",\"translation\":\"exemplified\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3644,\"bb\":3211,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3211/\",\"body_value\":\"The five great elements, false ego, intelligence, the unmanifested, the ten senses and the mind, the five sense objects, desire, hatred, happiness, distress, the aggregate, the life symptoms, and convictions – all these are considered, in summary, to be the field of activities and its interactions.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3645,\"bb\":3212,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3212/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3646,\"bb\":3213,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3213/\",\"body_value\":\"The five great elements are a gross representation of the false ego, which in turn represents the primal stage of false ego technically called the materialistic conception, or tāmasa-buddhi, intelligence in ignorance. This, further, represents the unmanifested stage of the three modes of material nature. The unmanifested modes of material nature are called pradhāna.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3647,\"bb\":3214,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3214/\",\"body_value\":\"One who desires to know the twenty-four elements in detail along with their interactions should study the philosophy in more detail. In Bhagavad-gītā, a summary only is given.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3648,\"bb\":3215,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/6-7/b3215/\",\"body_value\":\"The body is the representation of all these factors, and there are changes of the body, which are six in number: the body is born, it grows, it stays, it produces by-products, then it begins to decay, and at the last stage it vanishes. Therefore the field is a nonpermanent material thing. However, the kṣetra-jña, the knower of the field, its proprietor, is different.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 13.6-7\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 13.6-7\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Library\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/13/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",nu